msgid ""
"Using the automated valence active space procedure (AVAS) procedure is often"
" useful to generate a suitable starting guess for open-shell Hartree-Fock "
"calculations. If no previous orbitals are available, AVAS first uses an "
"atomic density guess to create initial orbitals, and these are the reordered"
" according to input specifications. For example, d-orbitals in transition "
"metal complexes can be rotated to the top of the occupied space. For more "
"details see section :doc:`Automated construction of atomic valence active "
"spaces <automated_construction_of_atomic_valence_active_spaces>`."
msgstr ""
"使用自动化价活性空间（AVAS）过程通常有助于为开壳层 Hartree-Fock 计算生成合适的初始猜测。如果之前没有可用的轨道，AVAS "
"首先使用原子密度猜测来创建初始轨道，然后根据输入规格对这些轨道重新排序。例如，过渡金属配合物中的 d 轨道可以被旋转到占据空间的顶部。更多细节参见章节 "
":doc:`Automated construction of atomic valence active spaces "
"<automated_construction_of_atomic_valence_active_spaces>`\\ 。"

msgid "``ROTATE,$orb_1.sym,orb_2.sym,angle$``"
msgstr "``ROTATE,$orb_1.sym,orb_2.sym,angle$``"

